{"name":"All Nighter","hex":"#455454","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"all nighter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of all-nighter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/all_nighter"}],"entries":[{"title":"All Nighter (film)","blocks":[{"text":"All Nighter is a 2017 American comedy film directed by Gavin Wiesen and written by Seth W. Owen. The film stars J. K. Simmons, Emile Hirsch, and Kristen Schaal. Principal photography began on July 6, 2015, on locations in Los Angeles, California."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/All_Nighter_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Nighter_(film)","wikidata":"Q20814835"},{"title":"All Nighter (bus service)","blocks":[{"text":"The All Nighter is a night bus service network in the San Francisco Bay Area, California. Portions of the service shadow the rapid transit and commuter rail services of BART and Caltrain, which are the major rail services between San Francisco, the East Bay, the Peninsula, and San Jose. Neither BART nor Caltrain operate owl service due to overnight track maintenance; the All Nighter network helps fill in this service gap. The slogan is, \"Now transit stays up as late as you do!\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ca/Allnighter-511.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Nighter_(bus_service)","wikidata":"Q4729185"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/All_Nighter_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/All_Nighter_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAll_Nighter_poster.jpeg